    "result_text": "Done. Here's what I implemented and the honest test status.\n\n## Change\n\nIn `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, in addition to the existing human-readable audit line, I now emit an immutable structured JSON event via the `AUDIT` logger on each successful create:\n\n```json\n{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nDetails:\n- **`seq`** \u2014 a static `AtomicLong` (`AUDIT_EVENT_SEQ`) incremented per create, so the sequence is monotonic across all creates.\n- **Primary identifier** \u2014 the `customerCode` field is sourced through a single `primaryIdentifier(owner)` seam that returns `owner.getCustomerCode()` today. Per the spec's forward-looking note, that one method is the only place to change when the identifier is unified into `memberId`, so the event will then carry the `memberId` instead \u2014 no other code touches it.\n- The JSON is built with a small `jsonString` escaper so identifier values are safely quoted/escaped.\n\nThe new `Cp53Tests.coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` passes (asserts one AUDIT line contains `OWNER_CREATED`, the owner id, and the `customerCode`).\n\n## Test suite status\n\nFull run: **65 tests, 2 failures** \u2014 `Cp23Tests.coreHouseholdAddsPoints` and `Cp39Tests.coreNewOwnerCappedBelowFour`, both failing on `$.membershipLevel expected:<3> but was:<2>`.\n\nThese are **pre-existing failures unrelated to this change**. I verified this by removing my `AUDIT.info(...)` event line and re-running: the same two tests fail identically. They concern the membership-level scoring/household-capping logic, not the audit event. I did not touch that logic, and I introduced no regressions \u2014 the failure set is byte-for-byte identical before and after my change.\n\nI left those two alone deliberately: fixing membership scoring is out of scope for this audit-event task, and this repo is a degradation-test harness where that logic was degraded by an earlier checkpoint. If you'd like, I can dig into the membership-scoring bug as a separate task.",
